##### crates/assistant_slash_command/src

Slash command framework, registry, working set, and extension bridging to expose commands in the assistant.

**Files:**

- `crates/assistant_slash_command/src/assistant_slash_command.rs` (rel=5): Core slash command framework defining the SlashCommand trait, argument completion behavior, event/content types, and the SlashCommandOutput with segmentation logic to convert text/sections to an event stream and back. It initializes the registry and extension bridge and provides parsing utilities for command lines.
- `crates/assistant_slash_command/src/slash_command_registry.rs` (rel=5): Defines a global registry for slash commands, tracking all commands and a featured subset with thread-safe registration, lookup, and unregistration. It is the central repository for discovering available commands by name.
- `crates/assistant_slash_command/src/extension_slash_command.rs` (rel=4): Bridges extension-provided slash commands into the core registry and adapts an LspAdapterDelegate to an extension WorktreeDelegate for file/system utilities. It forwards argument completion and execution to the extension host and maps returned sections to the core output format.
- `crates/assistant_slash_command/src/slash_command_working_set.rs` (rel=4): Maintains a per-panel working set of slash commands (e.g., context server commands), merging them with the global registry and tracking by ID and name. It updates internal name mappings on changes to support lookups within a panel instance.

#### crates/assistant_slash_commands

Crate exposing assistant slash commands integrated with the UI/editor.

##### crates/assistant_slash_commands/src

Slash commands (files/selection/tabs/prompts/fetch/diagnostics/delta/cargo workspace) with argument completion and section rendering.

**Files:**

- `crates/assistant_slash_commands/src/file_command.rs` (rel=5): Provides a slash command to complete and insert files/directories using fuzzy matching across visible worktrees, recent history, and glob patterns, streaming results as structured sections. It traverses project snapshots, auto-folds directories, builds rich completion labels, and uses code fences and path styles to render file contents or directory listings.
- `crates/assistant_slash_commands/src/context_server_command.rs` (rel=4): Slash command that binds to a ContextServer prompt, performing argument completion via server RPC and executing prompts to return aggregated user-message text. It enforces single-argument constraints, normalizes line endings, and labels/menu based on server/prompt metadata, with a helper to filter acceptable prompts.
- `crates/assistant_slash_commands/src/delta_command.rs` (rel=4): Slash command that re-runs prior file commands for unique paths and compares their outputs to detect changes, emitting only updated sections. It extracts metadata from previous sections, spawns concurrent recomputations, and aggregates diffs when changes are found.
- `crates/assistant_slash_commands/src/diagnostics_command.rs` (rel=4): Slash command that generates a project diagnostics summary with optional warnings and path filtering, and offers fuzzy completion for file paths and flags. It collects per-file summaries, formats grouped output using user-friendly path styles, and opens buffers as needed to extract ranges.
- `crates/assistant_slash_commands/src/fetch_command.rs` (rel=4): Defines a slash command that fetches a URL, detects Content-Type, and converts HTML to Markdown (with special Wikipedia handlers), or returns plaintext/pretty-printed JSON. It performs network I/O, error handling for HTTP status and headers, and streams the resulting text as a single labeled section.
- `crates/assistant_slash_commands/src/prompt_command.rs` (rel=4): Provides a slash command to search and insert a saved prompt from the PromptStore by title, with argument completion based on store search. It loads the prompt body asynchronously, normalizes edge cases (leading slash, empty body), and enables running nested commands within the inserted text.
- `crates/assistant_slash_commands/src/selection_command.rs` (rel=4): Adds a slash command that captures current editor selections and renders them as sections with appropriate formatting: code fences by language or blockquotes for Markdown, optional breadcrumbs from symbols, and titles with file path and line ranges. It aggregates multiple selections and streams them with spacing between sections.
- `crates/assistant_slash_commands/src/tab_command.rs` (rel=4): Implements a slash command to insert contents of open tabs (active or all), with argument completion that suggests the active tab, 'all', and fuzzy-matched open files ordered by recent activation. It gathers BufferSnapshots, matches queries strictly or fuzzily, and appends each buffer to the output with proper labeling and theming.

#### crates/assistant_tool

Shared tool plumbing crate used by agent and assistant UI.

##### crates/assistant_tool/src

Core tool abstractions (Tool, ToolCard/Result, sources) and working set management across native/MCP tools.

**Files:**

- `crates/assistant_tool/src/assistant_tool.rs` (rel=5): Defines the core tool abstractions including Tool, ToolCard, ToolResult, and ToolUseStatus, integrating with gpui entities and language models to run tools and render optional UI cards. It also models tool sources (native vs context server) and provides serialization hooks for card deserialization.
- `crates/assistant_tool/src/outline.rs` (rel=4): Generates and renders symbol outlines for large files by waiting for parse completion and formatting entries with line ranges, including pagination and optional regex filtering. Provides a utility to return either full buffer content or an outline based on size thresholds.
- `crates/assistant_tool/src/tool_registry.rs` (rel=4): Implements a global, thread-safe registry for tools with registration, unregistration, and lookup by name, backed by a hashmap in an RwLock. Offers App-global initialization and retrieval APIs to manage available tools.
- `crates/assistant_tool/src/tool_schema.rs` (rel=4): Adapts JSON schemas to specific language model formats by preprocessing (e.g., defaulting additionalProperties, ensuring properties) or transforming to a subset (e.g., removing unsupported keys, converting oneOf to anyOf) with recursive handling and tests. Ensures tool input schemas are compatible across providers.
- `crates/assistant_tool/src/tool_working_set.rs` (rel=4): Manages a working set of tools per Assistant instance, merging native tools with context-server tools and resolving name conflicts by prefixing context server IDs and truncation. Provides queries by source, insertion/removal, and conflict resolution with tests.

#### crates/assistant_tools

Crate aggregating assistant tools with templating and streaming diffs.

**Files:**

- `crates/assistant_tools/Cargo.toml` (rel=4): Aggregates assistant tools for editing, terminal use, web search, and diffs, integrating templating and streaming diffs with optional evaluation features.

##### crates/assistant_tools/src

Assistant tools registry and implementations for editing, terminal (sync/async), web search, diagnostics, FS ops, token usage.

**Files:**

- `crates/assistant_tools/src/assistant_tools.rs` (rel=5): Central module that exports types and registers the suite of tools into the ToolRegistry, conditionally enabling web search based on the default model provider and subscribing to model changes. Includes tests validating JSON Schema subset compatibility and tool registration for context tools.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/edit_agent.rs` (rel=5): Coordinates model-driven file edits (create, overwrite, granular edit) by constructing prompts, streaming and parsing edit chunks, and applying changes to buffers. Updates the ActionLog and agent location, resolves old text ranges, and emits edit events and output metrics.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/edit_file_tool.rs` (rel=5): Tool wrapper for editing/creating/overwriting files via EditAgent, handling path resolution, confirmation heuristics for sensitive locations, UI text, and LSP formatting triggers. Returns old/new text and raw agent output, optionally initializing UI card views.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/enhanced_terminal_tool.rs` (rel=5): Defines the core enhanced terminal infrastructure: global job registry, job ID generation, default and large output limits, denylist construction from settings, and dangerous command detection. Provides the minimal headless tool input/schema and shared utilities used by async/status/list tools.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/context_management.rs` (rel=4): Facilitates assistant context management by organizing chat history adapters/operations, list history, and memory tools via re-exports. Acts as a façade tying together state and memory tooling.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/copy_path_tool.rs` (rel=4): Assistant tool that copies a project file or directory to a destination path, validating project-relative paths and executing the copy asynchronously. It provides a JSON schema, descriptive UI text, and returns a confirmation message.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/create_directory_tool.rs` (rel=4): Assistant tool that creates a directory inside the project after verifying the path is within roots, performing the operation asynchronously and returning a confirmation. It includes JSON schema and UI text generation.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/delete_path_tool.rs` (rel=4): Assistant tool that deletes a file or directory with confirmation, traverses entries to log buffer deletions, opens relevant buffers for action logging, and performs the project delete operation. It streams paths from the worktree snapshot and reports completion.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/detect_binaries_tool.rs` (rel=4): Scans PATH for categorized developer binaries with bounded thread concurrency and per-binary version probing under a timeout, collecting presence, paths, versions, timing, and optional errors into a sorted report with summary. Requires confirmation and supports category filtering and privacy-minded path disclosure.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/diagnostics_tool.rs` (rel=4): Assistant tool that reports diagnostics for a specific file or summarizes project diagnostics, reading buffer snapshots and formatting error/warning messages by line. It supports optional path input and falls back to project-wide aggregation.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/enhanced_terminal_async_tool.rs` (rel=4): Runs commands asynchronously in a PTY with optional sudo, shell selection, env whitelist, and working directory resolution, enforcing safety via denylist and allow_dangerous policy from settings. Streams output into a global job registry with preview truncation and PID capture, returning a job id and background task output.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/enhanced_terminal_job_status_tool.rs` (rel=4): Reports status for async terminal jobs and optionally cancels them (best-effort SIGTERM/SIGKILL on Unix), returning JSON with state, runtime, exit code, and either preview or full output. Reads and updates the shared job registry.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/fetch_tool.rs` (rel=4): Assistant tool that fetches a URL via an HTTP client, detects content type, converts HTML to Markdown (with special Wikipedia handlers), pretty-prints JSON, or returns plaintext. It requires confirmation and produces formatted text for the model.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/find_path_tool.rs` (rel=4): Assistant tool that searches project paths using a glob with pagination and renders a tool card listing matches with jump-to-file actions. It supports deserializing output back into a card and runs path matching against worktree snapshots.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/grep_tool.rs` (rel=4): Assistant tool performing a regex search across project files with include/exclude globs respecting worktree and global settings, paginating results and extracting contextual or syntax-ancestor ranges. It streams search results and formats output per file with match grouping.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/list_directory_tool.rs` (rel=4): Assistant tool that lists contents of a project directory, filtering out private/excluded paths per global and worktree settings and separating folders from files, with special handling for root-like inputs. It returns a formatted listing or an error when paths are invalid.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/move_path_tool.rs` (rel=4): Assistant tool that moves or renames a project path to a destination, distinguishing renames when the parent directory is unchanged and executing the operation asynchronously. It validates project-relative paths and returns a status message.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/open_tool.rs` (rel=4): Assistant tool that opens a project path or URL with the system default application, resolving project-relative paths to absolute and confirming success. It includes tests for path resolution and requires confirmation.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/project_notifications_tool.rs` (rel=4): Assistant tool that surfaces unnotified user edits by summarizing diffs, compressing patches to fit a size budget, and outputting markdown with a header prompt, with tests for notification and compression logic. It flushes action log entries and formats multi-file changes.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/read_file_tool.rs` (rel=4): Assistant tool that reads a file or image from the project, honoring global/worktree exclusions and privacy, supports line-range selections and sets agent location, and returns text or image payload depending on model capabilities. It falls back to generating an outline for large files.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/save_context_tool.rs` (rel=4): Writes the current request’s full message history to a project file in markdown or JSON, deriving a default path from the worktree and sanitized title and validating paths remain inside the project. Assembles metadata and human-readable previews alongside raw JSON content.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/schema.rs` (rel=4): Generates JSON Schema for tool inputs using schemars with specialized settings and a transform that flattens type arrays and replaces oneOf with anyOf, then adapts it to the target language model format. This central utility ensures schema compatibility across tools and providers.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/templates.rs` (rel=4): Provides a Handlebars-based templating engine with embedded .hbs assets and a Template trait to render any serializable data. It registers an identity escape function to avoid HTML escaping and returns an Arc to share the compiled registry.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/terminal_tool.rs` (rel=4): Executes a command via PTY either headlessly or embedded in a TerminalView, building environment and shell context, normalizing and limiting captured output, and rendering a rich UI card for interactive sessions. Integrates with project/workspace and supports cross-platform shells.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/web_search_tool.rs` (rel=4): Provides a web search tool that queries an active provider asynchronously and returns serialized results plus structured output, with a UI card rendering clickable result titles and deserialization support for persisted cards. Integrates with the workspace and tool status lifecycle.

###### crates/assistant_tools/src/context_management

Global adapter to chat_history tools and a MemoryBackend API with tooling to list and mutate thread segments.

**Files:**

- `crates/assistant_tools/src/context_management/chat_history_tool.rs` (rel=4): Provides a global adapter to ChatHistoryTools and an internally-tagged ChatHistoryOperation enum covering append, search, answer, similar, list, get, create/delete chat, reembed, metadata updates, and config operations. Includes tests for schema generation and adapter installation, enabling a tool bridge to external chat history APIs.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/context_management/memory_ops.rs` (rel=4): Defines the MemoryBackend trait for thread-backed storage of conversation segments (list, stats, store, load, restore) using a foreground App reference, with a Noop implementation as default. Provides a gpui Global wrapper and accessor to install and retrieve the active backend instance.
- `crates/assistant_tools/src/context_management/memory_tool.rs` (rel=4): Implements the "memory" Tool that executes list/stats/store/load/restore operations via the global MemoryBackend, returning Markdown with JSON metadata and, when requested, stored messages. It performs mutations for store/restore synchronously to supply &mut App to the backend and may edit thread state.

