- `crates/denoise/src/engine.rs` (rel=4): Implements a real-time denoising engine using two embedded DTLN ONNX models, performing FFT-based magnitude/phase analysis, mask application, IFFT reconstruction, and maintaining recurrent memory tensors across blocks. Processes audio in fixed-size shifts, updating internal buffers to produce denoised output incrementally.
- `crates/denoise/src/lib.rs` (rel=4): Provides a rodio Source wrapper that runs the denoising Engine on a background thread, managing startup latency, enable/disable transitions, and a fixed-delay queue to preserve timing when bypassed. Splits input into sub-blocks, coordinates cross-thread I/O via channels, and yields denoised samples through Iterator.

