- `crates/settings/src/settings_file.rs` (rel=4): Provides async watchers for a settings file or directory using Fs and BackgroundExecutor, streaming file contents on changes via mpsc. Includes test_settings to produce a default JSON with platform-specific fonts and an empty theme, and delegates updates to SettingsStore.
- `crates/settings/src/settings_json.rs` (rel=4): Utilities to update and replace values in JSON text while preserving formatting/comments using tree-sitter queries, computing edit ranges and constructing nested objects when keys are missing. Handles removal with comma/whitespace adjustments and pretty-prints new values with controlled indentation.
- `crates/settings/src/vscode_import.rs` (rel=4): Loads and parses VS Code or Cursor user settings from known paths with lenient JSON, exposing typed accessors (string, bool, numeric, enum) and CSS-style font family parsing. Errors are contextualized with source and path information.

###### crates/settings/src/settings_content

Typed settings content models: agent, editor, language, language model providers, project, terminal, theme, workspace, extension capabilities.

**Files:**

- `crates/settings/src/settings_content/language.rs` (rel=5): Aggregates global and per-language settings with a merge_from algorithm that overlays defaults, global user settings, and language-specific overrides. Includes edit prediction providers/modes and many language formatting, wrapping, and tooling options.
- `crates/settings/src/settings_content/project.rs` (rel=5): ProjectSettingsContent combines language/worktree defaults with per-project LSP/DAP configuration, terminal settings, context servers, direnv, slash commands, and Git settings. Provides enums and helper setters for enabling, overriding, and safely redacting environment values.
- `crates/settings/src/settings_content/agent.rs` (rel=4): Defines AgentSettingsContent and related types for configuring the AI agent, including default models, profiles, permissions, notifications, and model parameters. Provides setters for common fields and enums for views and completion modes.
- `crates/settings/src/settings_content/editor.rs` (rel=4): Defines comprehensive editor UI and behavior settings (cursor, highlights, toolbars, scrollbars, minimap, gutter, search, signatures, contrast, diagnostics) with structured sub-settings and enums. Serves as the main abstraction for editor customization.
- `crates/settings/src/settings_content/language_model.rs` (rel=4): Defines settings for multiple language model providers (Anthropic, Bedrock, OpenAI, etc.), describing available models, capabilities, API endpoints, and parameters. Enables provider-specific customization and discovery of model features like tools, images, and thinking.
- `crates/settings/src/settings_content/terminal.rs` (rel=4): Defines terminal settings for fonts, line height, cursor, blinking, scrollback history, toolbar/scrollbar, contrast, and project-level shell and working directory selection. Includes enums mapping behavior (Shell, WorkingDirectory, ShowScrollbar) and conversions for line height.
- `crates/settings/src/settings_content/theme.rs` (rel=4): Centralizes UI/buffer font configuration, sizes, weights, features, line heights, and theme/icon theme selection (static or dynamic with system mode), plus theme override mechanisms. Provides font family conversions and validation for custom line heights and code fade intensity.
- `crates/settings/src/settings_content/workspace.rs` (rel=4): Defines workspace-level UI and behavior (pane layout, autosave, restore policies, dialogs, tabs, window closing behavior, dock resizing, padding) and item/preview tab settings. Uses enums to express policies and directions for consistent layout control.

