- `docs/src/languages/cpp.md` (rel=4): Explains native C++ support with configurable clangd binaries/arguments, clang-format setup, project-level .clangd config, compile_commands generation, and debugging. Highlights flexible LSP and formatter control within Zed.
- `docs/src/languages/go.md` (rel=4): Describes native Go support with recommended gopls installation, default inlay hint options and overrides, and rich Delve debugging flows (package, tests, exec, attach). Also notes tree-sitter grammars for go.mod/sum/work.
- `docs/src/languages/javascript.md` (rel=4): Describes native JavaScript support, including formatting via TypeScript or external tools like Prettier, ESLint-driven code actions, JSX and JSDoc parsing, and built-in debugging for tasks/tests with example configs. Highlights Zed’s integrated LSP, formatter, and DAP pipeline for JS projects.

